<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Vijayabahu I</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1039–1110</span> · <a href="/centuries/11th-century">11th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Vijayabahu I was king of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sri-lanka">Sri Lanka</a> from 1055 to 1110. Leading resistance from the southern Kingdom of Ruhuna against the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/chola-empire">Chola Empire</a>, which had ruled northern Sri Lanka since the early 11th century, he drove out the Cholas and took <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/polonnaruwa">Polonnaruwa</a> in 1070, making it his capital. He restored <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/buddhism">Buddhism</a>, bringing monks from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/burma">Burma</a> to renew the ordination lineage, and repaired irrigation works.</p></div>
